PRELIMINARY REMARK: The using rules of the software MEFISTO

The using of the software Mefisto and its numerical results are FREE.
But, it is forbidden to trade the software without an agreement with the authors
who can be contacted by e-mail at perronnet@ann.jussieu.fr

More, any publication must mention the using of the software MEFISTO and
its access on the web at https://www.ljll.math.upmc.fr/perronnet/mefisto.gene.html

The RIGHT BEHAVIOUR of the software is NEVER GUARANTED.
Any damage, done by the using of the software, could never be the subject of
compensation.

Any try of installation implies that the User has accepted implictly this rules.
*******************************************************************************

Prerequisites on HARDWARE and SOFTWARE:
=======================================
The installation needs of 
- a PC under system LINUX or equivalent;
- a main memory of 1 giga-bytes;
- a disk memory of 1 giga-bytes to store the software and execution files;
- a graphic card with a definition of the display
  1024x768 or 1280x1024 or + (the Qt 6 backend handles colour management itself).

DOWNLOAD and INSTALL the SOURCE of MEFISTO
==========================================
Let DirMefisto (as $HOME) the directory which will receive the file mefistosource.tgz
This directory name is now refered DirMefisto
- Give it the write access right by
  chmod 777 DirMefisto
- With a navigator as Mozilla or Firefox or ... , go to the URL
  https://www.ljll.math.upmc.fr/perronnet/instalsource.php
- Download in DirMefisto the 2 files: 
  . instalsource.bash
  . mefistosource.tgz
- go to this directory with the command
  cd DirMefisto
- Type ./instalsource.bash   under bash and follow the statements... (language,...)
  Wait patiently because many subroutines are compiled and the binding is long...
- Give the access rights to DirMefisto
  chmod -R 755 DirMefisto

At the installation level, a problem may be:
- a no correct name (upper case, ...)
- a DirMefisto name with a blank character
- a not possible access to DirMefisto by incorrect access rights
- a not installed gcc / gfortran / g++ compiler (load them)
- a not installed Qt 6 development package (load qt6-base-dev and
  qt6-image-formats-plugins; cmake >= 3.16 is also required to build xvue/qt/)
- an environment variable MEFISTO=DirMefisto/mefisto not initialized
- an environment variable MEFISTOX=$HOME/mefistox not initialized
- a directory DirMefisto/bin   without shell-scripts INITIER MAILLER ... to reload

INSTALLATION OF A USER OF MEFISTO:
==================================
instalsource.bash modifies the  personal file .bashrc in $HOME directory
by addition of the 2 environment variables

export MEFISTO=DirMefisto/mefistosource
export MEFISTOX=$HOME/mefistox

and after the definition of PATH and before the command export PATH, add
export PATH=.:$PATH:$MEFISTO/bin
export CDPATH=.:$HOME:$MEFISTO:$MEFISTOX

Then, under Linux, the typing of commands INITIER, MAILLER, ELASTICER, FLUIDER,
NLSER, THERMICER, cbl_tout, ...  will be found.

QUICK START (after install + env vars exported):
================================================
  INITIER             # create a project; type a project name when prompted
  MAILLER             # mesh: type same project name -> Qt window opens
  ELASTICER           # elasticity solver
  FLUIDER             # fluid solver
  THERMICER           # thermal solver
  NLSER               # nonlinear solver
  WAVER               # wave solver

  Inside any module: navigate menus + canvas; type 99; in the main menu
  to save and exit. NEVER use Ctrl-C.

ADVANCED (direct binary launch — auto-batch on non-tty):
  $MEFISTO/pp/pp<module> <data-file>   # cd into $MEFISTOX/<project> first
  When stdin is not a TTY (Wayland session, KDE launcher, pipeline) the Qt
  port automatically sets MEFISTO_BATCH_X11=1 + MEFISTO_XVSOURIS_AUTOEXIT=1
  so Fortran takes the non-interactive batch path.

REMARK on the Qt 6 GRAPHICS BACKEND:
====================================
Since Phase 9 (git tag v1.0-pre-retire and beyond), Mefisto's graphics layer
is built on Qt 6. The legacy X11 backend (xvue/xvuelc.c) and the legacy
"convert" raster-tool shell-out have been retired. The runtime + build
dependencies are:

- gfortran (Fortran 77/95 + OpenMP)
- gcc and g++
- qt6-base-dev (provides Qt6Widgets, Qt6Gui, Qt6Core, Qt6PrintSupport, Qt6Test)
- qt6-image-formats-plugins (TIFF, WebP, ... for the Qt image-export path)
- ffmpeg (animated GIF export via XvueExport::saveGifTo)
- cmake (>= 3.16, drives the xvue/qt/ build)

On Debian / Ubuntu, all of the above can be installed with:
  sudo apt install gfortran gcc g++ qt6-base-dev qt6-image-formats-plugins \
                   ffmpeg cmake

Phase 9: X11 retirement (v1.0+)
-------------------------------
Starting at git tag v1.0-pre-retire, MEFISTO migrated from the legacy X11
graphics backend (xvue/xvuelc.c, ~3749 lines) to a Qt 6 backend (xvue/qt/).
The X11 path was kept alive in parallel for one release cycle for A/B
validation (Phase 8). After the A/B window closed, Phase 9 deleted:

- xvue/xvuelc.c + bin/ccxvue (the X11 backend)
- xvue/video1.f + videofin.f + videonm.f + 12 tracer LVIDEO blocks
  (the legacy "xwd -> convert -> .gif" animation pipeline; replaced by
  the Phase 7 XvueExport::saveGifTo ffmpeg path)
- bin/convertepsgif, bin/png2eps, bin/png2jpg (legacy raster-tool shell-outs)
- legacy bin/cb* X11-linker scripts and Makefile relics
- the X11 development library and the legacy raster-conversion tool from the
  dependency list

To rebuild from the pre-retirement code: git checkout v1.0-pre-retire.
That tag still ships the X11 path and its original bin/cbl_tout.

Single graphics backend post-Phase-9: Qt 6 via bin/cbl_tout.

